-- ============================================================================
-- PD8 ASSOCIATE DEEP SEED: Well Intervention, beginner tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: THE FIT AND THE GEOMETRY. Four of its six graded fields
-- are the four continuous members of ONE return object from `logLogSlope`
-- called on a whole raw history: the slope, the intercept, the fit quality and
-- the span. The other two, `pssDenominator` and `minimumSkin`, take no series
-- at all and no window at all. So this tier is exactly the part of the module
-- that has no window, no classifier and no verdict anywhere near it, and the
-- boundary is a seam in the code rather than a chapter break in a syllabus:
-- `logLogSlope` on a raw history knows nothing about wells, and the two
-- geometry functions know nothing about time.
--
-- THE ONE SENTENCE THE COURSE IS, STATED HERE FIRST BECAUSE THIS IS WHERE IT
-- IS STILL SIMPLE. A Chan diagnosis is a straight line fitted to part of a
-- plot. Everything the two tiers above teach follows from what a fitted line
-- does and does not licence you to say, and a learner who cannot fit the line
-- and name every member of what comes back cannot price any of it.
--
-- THE TIER IS GENUINELY SIMPLE AND SAYING SO IS PART OF THE COURSE. Ordinary
-- least squares of ln y against ln x. It is exact on a power law and the
-- published gate proves it: the oracle commits eleven points on y = a x^m and
-- the THEIL-SEN slope through them, the median of every pairwise slope, which
-- shares no mean, no square and no covariance with the engine's least squares,
-- and the two routes agree to machine precision on the published slope of 1.35
-- and its intercept. That is a real check and it is one of only two the oracle
-- makes. A tier that manufactured a paradox out of a straight line here would
-- be teaching a suspicion the code does not earn.
--
-- WHAT THE TIER MUST ESTABLISH BEFORE ANYTHING IS DIAGNOSED, AND IT IS THE
-- LARGEST LIMIT IN THE COURSE. FOR ANY POWER-LAW HISTORY THE RATIO AND ITS
-- DERIVATIVE HAVE THE SAME LOG-LOG SLOPE. The engine's own comment concedes it
-- in as many words: d(a t^m)/d(ln t) = m a t^m, so the two cannot be separated
-- by comparing their slopes against each other, and "the only thing that
-- separates ordinary displacement from channelling is HOW STEEP the climb is".
-- That is why `channellingSlope` sits at 1.3 and `ambiguousBand` at 0.25, and
-- why a THRESHOLD rather than a physics decides whether a squeeze is
-- recommended. The Associate tier is where that is said plainly, because the
-- Professional tier spends money on the comparison and the Expert tier prices
-- what the comparison cost.
--
-- FOUR THINGS THE TIER MUST NOT LET A LEARNER ASSUME.
--
--   A FIT QUALITY IS A STATEMENT ABOUT THE LINE AND NOT ABOUT THE WELL. An
--   r-squared near one says the points lie near a straight line in log-log
--   coordinates. It says nothing about whether a straight line was the right
--   thing to fit. The published coning history is the demonstration and it is
--   published: it is a plateau curve, not a power law, and the engine's least
--   squares returns -0.539955222 against the oracle's Theil-Sen -0.555098340,
--   a disagreement in the SECOND DECIMAL on data with no noise in it at all,
--   because two estimators weight a curved log-log trend differently. Both are
--   right about their own question. Neither is a measurement of a slope that
--   exists. A learner who reads an r-squared as a licence has already made the
--   mistake the two tiers above are built on.
--
--   THE FIT DROPS POINTS AND DOES NOT SAY SO. `logLogSlope` filters out every
--   point whose y is not strictly positive, then fits what is left, and the n
--   it returns is the count AFTER the drop. The digest's own demonstration is
--   six points handed in of which two are negative: it returns ok true, n = 4,
--   and a `spanDecades` of 0.903089987 for a set of points that actually cover
--   1.505149978 log cycles, so the reported span is 0.602059991 of a log cycle
--   short of what was handed in and nothing in the object says which points
--   went. This tier owns noticing that a returned n is not an input count. The
--   Expert tier owns what it costs when the dropped points are the evidence
--   for the other mechanism.
--
--   THE GEOMETRY GROUP FORGIVES A GUESS AT THE RADIUS AND FORGIVES NOTHING AT
--   THE SKIN. `pssDenominator` is ln(re/rw) - 3/4 + S and nothing else, and the
--   productivity index is inversely proportional to it. The 3/4 is the
--   pseudo-steady-state constant for a circular drainage area, not a fudge and
--   not adjustable. A TWENTYFOLD change in the drainage radius, from 500 to
--   10000 ft on the published wellbore radius, moves the zero-skin denominator
--   by 2.995732274, which one unit of skin more than covers. A drainage radius
--   is a guess and a logarithm forgives a guess; a skin is a measurement and
--   the group adds it undivided. That asymmetry is why a stimulation study is
--   a skin study and not a radius study.
--
--   AND A BARE NaN IS A FAILURE CONTRACT, NOT AN ANSWER. `pssDenominator`,
--   `minimumSkin` and `skinFromPiRatio` all return a BARE NaN for a wellbore
--   radius larger than the drainage radius, while `skinPiMultiplier`, on the
--   same bad geometry, returns an object with ok false and a sentence. Two
--   failure contracts in one module, and a NaN cannot be told from an answer
--   without a finite check at every call site. This tier STATES the contract.
--   The Expert tier prices it on an inverse that has no plausibility check of
--   its own and is the natural way to audit a vendor's claimed uplift.
--
-- WHAT `minimumSkin` IS AND WHAT IT IS NOT, BECAUSE THE MODULE ITSELF GETS
-- THIS BOUNDARY WRONG ONE TIER LATER. It is the skin at which the denominator
-- reaches ZERO and the productivity index goes infinite. That is the
-- arithmetic running out, not a well getting better, and it is a mathematical
-- floor rather than an achievable target. The module's own refusal text names a
-- completely different and much shallower limit, "about -3 to -5 on acid and
-- -5 to -6 on a fracture", and everything between that range and the floor is
-- accepted in silence. The Associate tier's job is to have said what the floor
-- MEANS clearly enough that the Expert tier's finding lands as a gap between
-- two limits rather than as a surprise.
--
-- WHAT THE ORACLE CHECKS, SAID HERE BEFORE ANYTHING ELSE IS SAID ABOUT IT.
-- `oracle_intervention.py` is a good oracle as far as it goes, and both of its
-- checks belong to this tier. It checks the log-log slope by Theil-Sen. It
-- checks the skin uplift by building a full radial Darcy rate in SI,
-- permeability in square metres and pressures in pascals, and dividing two
-- real flow rates against the engine's ratio of two dimensionless groups. Two
-- genuinely independent routes onto two pure arithmetic functions, and both
-- hold to machine precision on the five published skin pairs and the published
-- power law. Then it stops, and everything above this tier lives in that
-- silence. Saying what IS checked, first and without hedging, is what makes
-- the Expert tier's account of what is not checked a finding instead of a
-- grievance.
--
-- UNITS, AND THEY ARE THE MODULE'S OWN. Producing time in days, radii in ft, a
-- water-oil ratio a bare stb/stb ratio, a gas-oil ratio in scf/stb, water cut
-- in percent, skin and the pseudo-steady-state group dimensionless, spans in
-- log cycles. A LOG-LOG SLOPE CARRIES NO UNIT AT ALL: it is d ln y / d ln x
-- and giving it one is a mistake this tier has to stamp out early. And fit
-- quality is a FRACTION in this engine and a PERCENTAGE in its own error
-- messages, so every lesson that names one says which it means.
--
-- The only numbers that travel from this tier to the next are the well's own
-- stated history and its stated geometry. The tier above restates every one of
-- them from scratch.
-- ============================================================================

values ('intervention', 'beginner', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-a-well-that-makes-water","title":"A Well That Makes Water","lesson_keys":["l01-why-a-ratio-history-is-a-plot","l02-what-this-engine-models","l03-what-it-refuses","l04-five-functions-and-one-idea"]},{"key":"m02-the-straight-line","title":"The Straight Line","lesson_keys":["l01-least-squares-in-log-space","l02-the-slope","l03-the-intercept","l04-exact-on-a-power-law","l05-what-a-slope-does-not-carry"]},{"key":"m03-reading-the-fit","title":"Reading the Fit","lesson_keys":["l01-r-squared-is-about-the-fit","l02-the-span-in-log-cycles","l03-how-many-points-the-fit-used","l04-what-a-clean-fit-does-not-prove"]},{"key":"m04-the-geometry-group","title":"The Geometry Group","lesson_keys":["l01-one-group-decides-the-value","l02-a-drainage-radius-is-a-guess","l03-skin-adds-undivided","l04-the-floor-a-geometry-allows","l05-two-failure-contracts"]},{"key":"m05-four-pictures","title":"Four Pictures","lesson_keys":["l01-channelling-against-coning","l02-displacement-and-not-determined","l03-the-thresholds-are-boundaries","l04-treatable-and-not","l05-what-a-label-is-not"]},{"key":"m06-the-associate-reading","title":"The Associate Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-story-so-far","l02-working-the-capstone","l03-onward"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
on conflict (app_slug, tier) do update
  set structure = excluded.structure,
      content_version = excluded.content_version,
      active = true,
      updated_at = now();

delete from public.academy_quiz_questions
 where app_slug = 'intervention' and tier = 'beginner';

